+# Pinned snapshot of https://github.com/mozilla-l10n/android-l10n
+#
+# This file is the Android counterpart of assets/l10n-pin.txt and uses exactly
+# the same format and the same two mandatory keys, validated by
+# lw_brand_strings.py's read_pin()/verify_sha256() -- which are ports of
+# scripts/librewolf-patches.py's functions of the same names.
+#
+# What it pins, and what it does NOT pin.  The translated Fenix strings we
+# SHIP come from the Firefox source tarball, which is GPG-verified already:
+# mobile/android/fenix/l10n.toml has `basepath = "."`, so upstream syncs
+# android-l10n into in-tree res/values-*/strings.xml before it cuts a release.
+# Re-downloading them would add a second, weaker supply chain for bytes we
+# already have.
+#
+# What this archive IS used for is the brand-word list in brand-map.txt.  The
+# rewrite has to recognise the mark in every script a translator has written it
+# in -- Фајерфокс, فايرفوكس, ഫയർഫോക്സ്, ෆයර්ෆොක්ස්, ᱯᱷᱟᱭᱟᱨᱯᱷᱚᱠᱥ -- and that list
+# is derived from this corpus, which is a superset of the in-tree one (196
+# Fenix locales here against 131 in the tree). A tampered corpus produces a
+# brand map with a missing or a bogus stem, so it is verified before it is
+# unpacked, on the same principle as the desktop pin.
+#
+# Format: "key = value", one per line, '#' starts a comment.
+#   commit   full 40-hex commit sha in mozilla-l10n/android-l10n
+#   sha256   sha256 of https://codeload.github.com/mozilla-l10n/android-l10n/zip/<commit>
+#
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# HOW TO BUMP THIS PIN -- both lines, in this order:
+#
+#   1. Pick the commit:
+#        git ls-remote https://github.com/mozilla-l10n/android-l10n refs/heads/main
+#
+#   2. Download that exact archive and hash it:
+#        sha=<the 40-hex sha from step 1>
+#        curl -sfL -o /tmp/android-l10n.zip \
+#          "https://codeload.github.com/mozilla-l10n/android-l10n/zip/$sha"
+#        sha256sum /tmp/android-l10n.zip
+#
+#   3. Write both values below, then re-derive and review the brand map:
+#        python3 mobile/android/lw-brand/lw_brand_strings.py resync \
+#            --tree mobile/android
+#
+# The same caveat as assets/l10n-pin.txt applies: codeload generates these zips
+# on demand and GitHub does not contractually guarantee byte-stability. If the
+# sha256 check starts failing while the commit line is unchanged, extract both
+# archives and diff the trees before touching the hash. A hash refreshed
+# without looking is not a pin.
+#
+# Verified on 2026-08-19: two downloads of the commit below, minutes apart,
+# were byte-identical (15971521 bytes).
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+commit = b1b54243735917584168051b7206ca249427e86b
+sha256 = 637978a42324ce15acdf01b7691ddddf3cd7caec4fe33f834fb1badee472c8f9
